From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: dts: turris1x: rename the NAND partition to "ubi"

The NAND partition holds a UBI container whose rootfs volume carries the
root filesystem. With the partition itself called "rootfs",
CONFIG_MTD_ROOTFS_ROOT_DEV picks its mtdblock as the root device before
the ubiblock of the volume exists, and the kernel then looks for the
filesystem in the raw UBI container:

  ubi0: attached mtd7 (name "rootfs", size 256 MiB)
  block ubiblock0_1: created from ubi0:1(rootfs)
  No filesystem could mount root, tried: squashfs
  Kernel panic - not syncing: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on unknown-block(31,7)

Name the partition after what it contains, which is what the other NAND
boards in this target do, so that the volume can be selected by name and
the kernel command line does not have to spell out a volume number.

The name also opts the partition into the OpenWrt UBI auto-attach, which
runs on any boot that does not pass ubi.mtd= and uses the default VID
header offset. This UBI is written with 2048, the offset the factory
bootloader expects, so the attach fails and logs an error.

That failure is load-bearing rather than cosmetic. The boot it happens on
is the microSD one, which must not attach the NAND: mount_root prefers a
UBI rootfs_data over the one on the card, so a card system would store its
configuration in the NAND. The two media are therefore kept apart by the
offset mismatch, which is worth knowing before anyone reformats this NAND
with the default offset.

Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
+++ b/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
@@ -332,7 +332,7 @@
 				partition@0 {
 					/* 256 MB for UBI with one volume: UBIFS Root File System */
 					reg = <0x00000000 0x10000000>;
-					label = "rootfs";
+					label = "ubi";
 				};
 			};
 		};
